G4571.b:
⟪αὐτός⟫, -ή, -ό, determinative pron., in late Gk. much more freq. than in cl. (WM, 178 f.; Jannaris, HGG, §1399).
⟪1.⟫ Emphatic (so always in nom. exc. when preceded by the art., v. infr., iii);
	⟪(1)⟫ ⟪self⟫ (ipse), expressing opposition, distinction, exclusion, etc., αὐ. ἐκχυθήσεται, ⟦Luke 5:37|Lk 5:37⟧; αὐ. ἐγινώσκεν, ⟦John 2:25|Jo 2:25⟧; αὐ. ὑμεῖς, ⟦John 3:28|Jo 3:28⟧; καὶ αὐ. ἐγώ, ⟦Romans 15:14|Ro 15:14⟧; αὐ. Ἰησοῦς, ⟦John 2:24|Jo 2:24⟧; αὐ. καὶ οἱ μετ’ αὐτοῦ, ⟦Matthew 2:25|Mk 2:25⟧; ὑμεῖς αὐ., ⟦Mark 6:31|Mk 6:31⟧; esp. (as freq in cl.) αὐ. ὁ, ⟦Matthew 3:4|Mt 3:4⟧, ⟦Mark 6:17|Mk 6:17⟧, ⟦John 16:27|Jo 16:27⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:11|I Th 3:11⟧, al.; in late Gk., sometimes weakened, ἐν αὐτῇ τ. ὥρᾳ, ⟪in that hour⟫, ⟦Luke 10:21|Lk 10:21⟧ (M, Pr., 91; MM, s.v.);
	⟪(2)⟫ emphatic, ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫ (M, Pr., 86; Bl., § 48, 1, 2, 7), ⟦Matthew 1:21|Mt 1:21⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:50|12:50⟧, ⟦Luke 6:35|Lk 6:35⟧, al.; pointing to some one as master (cl.), ⟦Matthew 8:24|Mt 8:24⟧, ⟦Mark 4:38|Mk 4:38⟧, al.; αὐ., καὶ αὐ. = οὗτος, ὁ δε (Bl., § 48, 1), ⟦Matthew 14:2|Mt 14:2⟧, ⟦Mark 14:15|Mk 14:15⟧, ⟦Mark 14:44|44⟧, ⟦Luke 1:22|Lk 1:22⟧ ⟦Luke 2:28|2:28⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ In oblique cases (cl.), for the simple pron. of 3rd pers., ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫, ⟦Matthew 7:9|Mt 7:9⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:12|10:12⟧, ⟦Matthew 26:44|26:44⟧, al.; with ptcp. in gen. absol., ⟦Matthew 9:18|Mt 9:18⟧, ⟦Mark 13:1|Mk 13:1⟧, al. (for irreg. constructions, V. Bl., § 74, 5); pleonastically after the relative (cf. Heb. ⁨אֲשֶׁר לֹו⁩; WM, 184 ff.; Bl., § 50, 4; MM, s.v.), ⟦Mark 7:25|Mk 7:25⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:8|Re 3:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:2|7:2⟧, al.; in constr. ad sensum, without proper subject expressly indicated, ⟦Matthew 4:23|Mt 4:23⟧, ⟦Acts 8:5|Ac 8:5⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 2:13|II Co 2:13⟧, al.; gen. αὐτοῦ = ἐκείνου, ⟦Romans 11:11|Ro 11:11⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:19|I Th 2:19⟧, ⟦Titus 3:5|Tit 3:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:4|He 2:4⟧.
⟪3.⟫ ὁ, ἡ, τὸ αὐ., ⟪the same⟫: ⟦Hebrews 1:12|He 1:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:8|13:8⟧; τὸ αὐ., ποιεῖν, ⟦Matthew 5:46|Mt 5:46⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:47|47⟧, al.; φρονεῖν, ⟦Romans 12:16|Ro 12:16⟧ ⟦Romans 15:5|15:5⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:2|Phl 2:2⟧, al.; τὰ αὐ., ⟦Acts 15:27|Ac 15:27⟧, ⟦Romans 2:1|Ro 2:1⟧, al.; κατὰ τὸ (τὰ) αὐ. (MM, s.v.), ⟦Acts 14:1|Ac 14:1⟧, ⟦Luke 6:23|Lk 6:23⟧, al.; ἐπὶ τὸ αὐ., ⟪together⟫ (MM, s.v.), ⟦Matthew 22:34|Mt 22:34⟧, ⟦Acts 1:15|Ac 1:15⟧, al.; ἓν κ. τὸ αὐ., ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:11|12:11⟧; c. dat. (cl.), ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧; with a noun, λόγος, Mk 14:39; μέτρος, ⟦Philippians 1:30|Phl 1:30⟧; πνεῦμα, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:4|I Co 12:4⟧.

G4521.b:
† ⟪σάββατον⟫, -ου, τό (Aram. ⁨שַׁבָּתָא⁩, transliterated σάββατα, and this being mistaken for a pl., the sing. σάββατον was formed from it), and σάββατα, -ων, τά
[in LXX for ⁨שַׁבָּת⁩, ⁨שַׁבָּתוֹן⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪the seventh day⟫ of the week, ⟪the sabbath⟫
⟪(a)⟫ the sing. form -ον, τὸ σ.: ⟦Matthew 12:8|Mt 12:8⟧, ⟦Mark 2:27|Mk 2:27⟧, ⟦Luke 6:5|Lk 6:5⟧, al.; ἡ ἡμέρα τοῦ σ. (in LXX, ⟦Exodus 20:8|Ex 20:8⟧, al., usually τῶν σ., v. infr.), ⟦Luke 13:16|Lk 13:16⟧ ⟦Luke 14:5|14:5⟧; ὁδὸς σαββάτου, ⟦Acts 1:12|Ac 1:12⟧ (cf. ⟦Matthew 24:20|Mt 24:20⟧); dat., of time (τῷ) σ., ⟦Luke 6:9|Lk 6:9⟧ ⟦Luke 14:1|14:1⟧; ἐν (τῷ) σ., ⟦Matthew 12:2|Mt 12:2⟧, ⟦Luke 6:7|Lk 6:7⟧, ⟦John 5:16|Jo 5:16⟧, al.; acc., of duration, τὸ σ., ⟦Luke 23:56|Lk 23:56⟧; κατὰ πᾶν σ., ⟦Acts 13:27|Ac 13:27⟧ ⟦Acts 15:21|15:21⟧ ⟦Acts 18:4|18:4⟧; pl., σ. τρία, ⟦Acts 17:2|Ac 17:2⟧ R, txt. (but v. infr.);
⟪(b)⟫ as most freq. in LXX (v. Swete, Mk., 17; Thackeray, Gr., 35) the pl. form, τὰ σ. (v. supr. on the Aram. form. There is also an analogy in the names of other festivals, τ. ἐγκαίνια, ἄζυμα, etc.): ⟦Matthew 28:1|Mt 28:1⟧, ⟦Colossians 2:16|Col 2:16⟧; ἡ ἡμέρα τῶν σ. (⟦Exodus 20:8|Ex 20:8⟧, al.), ⟦Luke 4:16|Lk 4:16⟧, ⟦Acts 13:14|Ac 13:14⟧ ⟦Acts 16:13|16:13⟧; dat. pl. (in LXX -τοις, but I Mac 2:38 as in NT) by metaplasmus (Bl., § 9, 3), σάββασι, ⟦Matthew 12:1|Mt 12:1⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:5|5⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:10|10-12⟧ ⟦Mark 1:21|Mk 1:21⟧ ⟦Mark 2:23|2:23⟧ ⟦Mark 3:2|3:2⟧, ⟦Mark 3:4|4⟧, ⟦Luke 4:31|Lk 4:31⟧ ⟦Luke 6:2|6:2⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪seven days, a week⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ the sing. form: πρώτη σαββάτσυ, ⟦Mark 16:9|Mk 16:9⟧; δὶς τοῦ σ. (Bl., § 35, 4; 36, 13), ⟦Luke 18:12|Lk 18:12⟧; κατὰ μίαν σαββάτου, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:2|I Co 16:2⟧; pl., σ. τρία, ⟦Acts 17:2|Ac 17:2⟧ R, mg. (but v. supr.);
⟪(b)⟫ the pl. form: ἡ μία τῶν σ. (where the gen. = μετὰ τά; Soph., Lex., 43a), ⟦Matthew 28:1|Mt 28:1⟧, ⟦Mark 16:2|Mk 16:2⟧, ⟦Luke 24:1|Lk 24:1⟧, ⟦John 20:1|Jo 20:1⟧, ⟦John 20:19|19⟧, ⟦Acts 20:7|Ac 20:7⟧

G4526.b:
⟪σάκκος⟫ also written σάκος, -ου, ὁ
(cf. Heb. ⁨שַׂק⁩, which it renders in LXX),
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a coarse cloth, sackcloth⟫, usually made of hair: ⟦Revelation 6:12|Re 6:12⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Anything made of sackcloth;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a sack⟫ (⟦Genesis 42:25|Ge 42:25⟧, al.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a garment of sackcloth⟫, expressive of mourning or penitence: ⟦Matthew 11:21|Mt 11:21⟧, ⟦Luke 10:13|Lk 10:13⟧, ⟦Revelation 11:3|Re 11:3⟧.†

G4531.b:
⟪σαλεύω⟫
(< σάλος), [in LXX for ⁨מוּט⁩, ⁨נוּעַ⁩, etc. ;] prop., of the action of wind, storm, etc., ⟪to agitate, shake⟫: of a reed, ⟦Matthew 11:7|Mt 11:7⟧, ⟦Luke 7:24|Lk 7:24⟧; a house, ⟦Luke 6:48|Lk 6:48⟧, ⟦Acts 4:31|Ac 4:31⟧ ⟦Acts 16:26|16:26⟧; the earth, ⟦Hebrews 12:26|He 12:26⟧; the heavenly bodies, ⟦Matthew 24:29|Mt 24:29⟧, ⟦Mark 13:25|Mk 13:25⟧, ⟦Luke 21:26|Lk 21:26⟧; of a vessel shaken in filling, ⟦Luke 6:38|Lk 6:38⟧. Metaph.,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to shake⟫, i.e. to render insecure: τὰ σαλευόμενα, τὰ μὴ., ⟦Hebrews 12:27|He 12:27⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ c. acc pers., ⟪to cast down⟫ from a sense of security and happiness: ⟦Acts 2:25|Ac 2:25⟧ (LXX);
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to unsettle⟫ or ⟪drive away⟫: pass., seq. ἀπὸ τ. νοός, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:2|II Th 2:2⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ ⟪to stir up⟫: τ. ὄχλους, ⟦Acts 17:13|Ac 17:13⟧.†

G4540.b:
⟪Σαμαρία⟫ (Rec. -άρεια), -ας, ἡ (Heb. ⁨שֹׁמְרוֹן⁩; Aram. ⁨שָׁמְרַיִן⁩), ⟪Samaria⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ the city: ⟦Acts 8:5|Ac 8:5⟧ (and perhaps also ⟦Acts 8:9|9⟧, ⟦Acts 8:14|14⟧);
⟪(b)⟫ the region: ⟦Luke 17:11|Lk 17:11⟧, ⟦John 4:4|Jo 4:4, 5⟧, ⟦John 4:7|7⟧, ⟦Acts 1:8|Ac 1:8⟧ ⟦Acts 8:1|8:1⟧ (and perhaps also ⟦Acts 8:9|8:9⟧, ⟦Acts 8:14|14⟧) ⟦Acts 9:31|9:31⟧ ⟦Acts 15:3|15:3⟧.†

G4549.b:
⟪Σαούλ⟫, ὁ indecl.
(in FlJ, Σάουλος; Heb. ⁨שָׁאוּל⁩) ⟪Saul⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ the King of Israel: ⟦Acts 13:21|Ac 13:21⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ the Jewish name of the Apostle Paul, used in the indecl. form only in address (cf. Σαῦλος): ⟦Acts 9:4|Ac 9:4⟧, ⟦Acts 9:17|17⟧ ⟦Acts 22:7|22:7⟧, ⟦Acts 22:13|13⟧ ⟦Acts 26:14|26:14⟧.†

G4561.b:
⟪σάρξ⟫, σαρκός, ἡ
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨בָּשָׂר⁩ ;] ⟪flesh⟫;
⟪1.⟫ as in cl. generally,
	⟪(a)⟫ prop., of the soft substance of the animal body: ⟦1 Corinthians 15:39|I Co 15:39⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:7|II Co 12:7⟧, ⟦Galatians 6:13|Ga 6:13⟧, al.; σ. καὶ αἷμα, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:50|I Co 5:50⟧; σ. καὶ ὀστέα, ⟦Luke 24:39|Lk 24:39⟧; pl., of the flesh of many or parts of the flesh of one (cl.), ⟦Revelation 17:16|Re 17:16⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:18|19:18⟧; φαγεῖν, Re, ll. c. (cf. κατεσθίειν, ⟦2 Kings 9:36|IV Ki 9:36⟧, al., and βιβρώσκειν, freq. in l.); metaph., ⟦James 5:3|Ja 5:3⟧; mystically, φ. (τρώγειν) τὴν σ. τοῦ υἱοῦ τ. ἀνθρώπου, ⟦John 6:52|Jo 6:52-56⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ Of the whole substance of the body, = σῶμα: ⟦Acts 2:26|Ac 2:26⟧ (LXX), ⟦Acts 2:31|31⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:7|II Co 12:7⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:14|Ga 4:14⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:29|Eph 5:29⟧; μία σ., ⟦Mark 10:8|Mk 10:8⟧; εἰς σ. μίαν (⟦Genesis 2:24|Ge 2:24⟧), ⟦Matthew 19:5|Mt 19:5⟧, ⟦Mark 10:8|Mk 10:8⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 6:16|I Co 6:16⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:31|Eph 5:31⟧; hence, of the material as opp. to the immaterial part of man (cf. Lft., Notes, 88): opp. to πνεῦμα, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:5|I Co 5:5⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 7:1|II Co 7:1⟧, ⟦Colossians 2:5|Col 2:5⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:18|I Pe 3:18⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:6|4:6⟧; to ψύχη, ⟦Acts 2:31|Ac 2:31⟧, Rec.; of the present life, ἐν (τῇ) σ., ⟦Romans 7:5|Ro 7:5⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:20|Ga 2:20⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:22|Phl 1:22⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:24|24⟧ ⟦1 Peter 4:2|I Pe 4:2⟧; of Christ's life on earth, αἱ ἡμέραι τ. σαρκὸς αὐτοῦ, ⟦Hebrews 5:7|He 5:7⟧; of things pertaining to the body, ἐν (τῇ) σ., ⟦Galatians 6:12|Ga 6:12⟧, ⟦Galatians 6:13|13⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:3|Phl 3:3⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:4|4⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As in Heb. idiom,
	⟪(a)⟫ of a living creature: πᾶσα σ. (Heb. ⁨כָּל־בָּשָׂר⁩; cf. Bl., § 47, 9), ⟦Matthew 24:22|Mt 24:22⟧, ⟦Mark 13:20|Mk 13:20⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:24|I Pe 1:24⟧; esp. of man and his mortality (Ps 55 (56):5, Si 28:5, al.), ⟦John 1:14|Jo 1:14⟧; πᾶσα σ. (v. supr.), ⟦Luke 3:6|Lk 3:6⟧, ⟦John 17:2|Jo 17:2⟧, ⟦Acts 2:17|Ac 2:17⟧, ἐν σ., ⟦1 John 4:2|I Jo 4:2⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:16|I Ti 3:16⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of natural origin and relationship (⟦Genesis 2:24|Ge 2:24⟧, ⟦Isaiah 58:7|Is 58:7⟧, al.): τέκνα τῆς σ., ⟦Romans 9:8|Ro 9:8⟧; κατὰ σάρκα, ⟦Romans 9:3|ib. 3⟧, ⟦Romans 9:5|5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:18|I Co 10:18⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:23|Ga 4:23⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:29|29⟧; ἡ σ. μου, ⟦Romans 11:14|Ro 11:14⟧ (cf. ⟦Judges 9:2|Jg 9:2⟧, ⟦2 Samuel 5:1|II Ki 5:1⟧, al.).
⟪3.⟫ Of the physical nature as subject to sensation and desire (Plut.),
	⟪(a)⟫ without any ethical disparagement: ⟦Romans 7:18|Ro 7:18⟧ ⟦Romans 13:14|13:14⟧; opp. to πνεῦμα, ⟦Matthew 26:41|Mt 26:41⟧, ⟦Mark 14:38|Mk 14:38⟧; τ. θέλημα τῆς σ., ⟦John 1:13|Jo 1:13⟧; ἡ ἐπιθυμία τῆς σ., ⟦1 John 2:16|I Jo 2:16⟧; pl., ⟦2 Peter 2:18|II Pe 2:18⟧; παθεῖν σαρκί, ⟦1 Peter 4:1|I Pe 4:1⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ in ethical sense, esp. in Pauline Epp., of the flesh as the seat and vehicle of sinful desires: opp. to νοῦς, ⟦Romans 7:25|Ro 7:25⟧; to πνεῦμα, ⟦Romans 8:4|Ro 8:4-9⟧, ⟦Romans 8:12|12⟧, ⟦Romans 8:13|13⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:16|Ga 5:16⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:17|17⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:19|19⟧ ⟦Galatians 6:8|6:8⟧ (cf. DB, ii, 14f.; iv, 165f.; Cremer, 844 ff.).

G4575.b:
* ⟪σεβαστός⟫, -ή, -όν (σεβάζομαι)
⟪1.⟫ ⟪reverend, august⟫.
⟪2.⟫ In late writers, with reference to the Roman Imperial name;
⟪(a)⟫ ὁ Σ., ⟪Augustus⟫, i.e. the Roman Emperor: ⟦Acts 25:21|Ac 25:21⟧, ⟦Acts 25:25|25⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪Augustan⟫: σπείρα σ., ⟦Acts 27:1|Ac 27:1⟧ (See further, Deiss., BS, 218.) †

G4592.b:
⟪σημεῖον⟫, -ου, τό
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אוֹת⁩ ;] ⟪a sign, mark, token⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of that which distinguishes a person or thing from others: ⟦Matthew 26:48|Mt 26:48⟧, ⟦Luke 2:12|Lk 2:12⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 3:17|II Th 3:17⟧ (cf. Deiss., LAE, 1532); seq. gen. epexeg., ⟦Romans 4:11|Ro 4:11⟧; c. gen. obj., ⟦Matthew 24:8|Mt 24:8⟧, ⟦Matthew 24:30|30⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:12|II Co 12:12⟧; c. gen. subj., ⟦Matthew 16:3|Mt 16:3⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ a sign of warning or admonition: ⟦Matthew 12:39|Mt 12:39⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:4|16:4⟧, ⟦Luke 2:34|Lk 2:34⟧ ⟦Luke 11:29|11:29, 30⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:22|I Co 14:22⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ a sign portending future events (Soph., Plat. al.): ⟦Mark 13:4|Mk 13:4⟧, ⟦Luke 21:7|Lk 21:7⟧, ⟦Luke 21:11|11⟧, ⟦Luke 21:25|25⟧, ⟦Acts 2:19|Ac 2:19⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:1|Re 12:1⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:3|3⟧ ⟦Revelation 15:1|15:1⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ of miracles and wonders (MM, xxii), regarded as signs of a divine authority: ⟦Matthew 12:38|Mt 12:38, 39⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:1|16:1⟧, ⟦Matthew 16:4|4⟧, ⟦Mark 8:11|Mk 8:11, 12⟧ ⟦Luke 11:16|Lk 11:16⟧, ⟦Luke 11:29|29⟧ ⟦Luke 23:8|23:8⟧, ⟦John 2:11|Jo 2:11⟧, ⟦John 2:18|18⟧, ⟦John 2:23|23⟧ ⟦John 4:54|4:54⟧ ⟦John 6:30|6:30⟧ ⟦John 10:41|10:41⟧ ⟦John 12:18|12:18⟧, ⟦Acts 4:16|Ac 4:16⟧, ⟦Acts 4:22|22⟧; pl., ⟦Mark 16:17|Mk 16:[17⟧, ⟦Mark 16:20|20]⟧, ⟦John 2:11|Jo 2:11⟧, ⟦John 2:23|23⟧ ⟦John 3:2|3:2⟧ ⟦John 6:2|6:2⟧, ⟦John 6:14|14⟧, ⟦John 6:26|26⟧ ⟦John 7:31|7:31⟧ ⟦John 9:16|9:16⟧ ⟦John 11:47|11:47⟧ ⟦John 12:37|12:37⟧ ⟦John 20:30|20:30⟧, ⟦Acts 8:6|Ac 8:6⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:22|I Co 1:22⟧ (Lft., Notes, 162); the same ascribed to false teachers and demons: ⟦Matthew 24:24|Mt 24:24⟧, ⟦Mark 13:22|Mk 13:22⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:9|II Th 2:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 13:13|Re 13:13, 14⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:14|16:14⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:20|19:20⟧; σ. καὶ τέρατα (τ. καὶ σ.; cf. Tr., Syn., § xci), ⟦Matthew 24:24|Mt 24:24⟧, ⟦Mark 13:22|Mk 13:22⟧, ⟦John 4:48|Jo 4:48⟧, ⟦Acts 2:19|Ac 2:19⟧, ⟦Acts 2:43|43⟧ ⟦Acts 4:30|4:30⟧ ⟦Acts 5:12|5:12⟧ ⟦Acts 6:8|6:8⟧ ⟦Acts 7:36|7:36⟧ ⟦Acts 14:3|14:3⟧ ⟦Acts 15:12|15:12⟧, ⟦Romans 15:19|Ro 15:19⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:9|II Th 2:9⟧; id. seq. καὶ δυνάμεις, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:12|II Co 12:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:4|He 2:4⟧; σ. καὶ δυνάμεις, ⟦Acts 8:13|Ac 8:13⟧; δ. καὶ τ. καὶ σ., ⟦Acts 2:22|Ac 2:22⟧; σ. διδόναι, ⟦Matthew 24:24|Mt 24:24⟧, ⟦Mark 13:22|Mk 13:22⟧.†
